---
import SectionHeading from '../components/journal/SectionHeading.astro';
import InteriorPageLayout from '../layouts/InteriorPageLayout.astro';
---

<InteriorPageLayout
  title="About"
  description="Dipanjan Mondal is a software engineer writing about how software works and the tools he is building."
  eyebrow="Dipanjan Mondal"
  lede="I’m a software engineer. I explain how software works and share the tools I’m building to make it better."
  contentFirst
  rail={{
    title: 'At a glance',
    items: [
      { label: 'Work', value: 'Software engineering' },
      { label: 'Interests', value: 'Software internals and tools for developers' },
      { label: 'Current project', value: 'Quill, a verifier prototype' },
    ],
  }}
>
  <div class="about-sections">
    <section aria-labelledby="about-subjects">
      <SectionHeading id="about-subjects" eyebrow="Writing" title="How software works" />
      <div class="about-prose">
        <p>
          I like understanding what happens underneath the interfaces we use every day: how a
          database stores an update, what survives a crash, or why concurrent operations can produce
          an unexpected result.
        </p>
        <p>
          Here I work through those questions with concrete examples, code, and interactive figures.
          The aim is to make the reasoning visible, so you can follow the decisions and see what
          each one changes.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="about-building">
      <SectionHeading
        id="about-building"
        eyebrow="Building"
        title="Tools to explore those questions"
      />
      <div class="about-prose">
        <p>
          I’m developing Quill, a verifier prototype, and exploring deterministic simulation
          testing. I’m interested in how we can control the conditions a system runs under and
          investigate failures that are hard to produce in ordinary testing.
        </p>
        <p>
          I’ll share the work as it develops: what a prototype can demonstrate, the decisions behind
          it, and the questions still open.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="about-follow">
      <SectionHeading id="about-follow" eyebrow="Elsewhere" title="Follow the work" />
      <nav class="about-links" aria-label="Follow the work">
        <a href="https://github.com/mdipanjan">
          <span>Code and projects</span><strong>GitHub</strong>
        </a>
        <a href="https://x.com/devdjm">
          <span>Short explanations and updates</span><strong>X · @devdjm</strong>
        </a>
        <a href="/archive/">
          <span>Browse the writing</span><strong>Archive</strong>
        </a>
        <a href="/rss.xml">
          <span>Get new articles in your reader</span><strong>RSS feed</strong>
        </a>
      </nav>
    </section>
  </div>
</InteriorPageLayout>

<style>
  .about-sections {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-8);
  }

  .about-sections > section + section {
    padding-top: var(--space-7);
    border-top: var(--border-thin) solid var(--color-rule);
  }

  .about-prose {
    max-width: var(--width-prose);
  }

  .about-prose p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: var(--font-size-body);
    line-height: var(--line-height-reading);
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  .about-prose p + p {
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
  }

  .about-links {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    border-block: var(--border-thin) solid var(--color-rule);
  }

  .about-links a {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    padding: var(--space-5);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .about-links a:nth-child(even) {
    border-left: var(--border-thin) solid var(--color-rule);
  }

  .about-links a:nth-child(n + 3) {
    border-top: var(--border-thin) solid var(--color-rule);
  }

  .about-links a:hover {
    background: var(--color-accent-soft);
  }

  .about-links span {
    font-size: var(--font-size-small);
  }

  .about-links strong {
    color: var(--color-accent);
    font-family: var(--font-interface);
    font-size: var(--font-size-label);
    font-weight: var(--weight-medium);
  }

  @media (max-width: 520px) {
    .about-links {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .about-links a + a {
      border-top: var(--border-thin) solid var(--color-rule);
      border-left: 0;
    }
  }
</style>
